=== tm-e1: SUM of a DATE MAX output is refused ===
Error handling: RPE
ronsql_cli caught exception: A CTE output that is a MIN or MAX of a DATE, DATETIME, TIME, TIMESTAMP or YEAR column can be used in an aggregate only as the argument of MIN or MAX, or in a GREATEST or LEAST whose arguments are all CTE outputs of the same temporal type and fractional precision.

=== tm-e2: MAX of arithmetic over a DATE MAX output is refused ===
Error handling: RPE
ronsql_cli caught exception: A CTE output that is a MIN or MAX of a DATE, DATETIME, TIME, TIMESTAMP or YEAR column can be used in an aggregate only as the argument of MIN or MAX, or in a GREATEST or LEAST whose arguments are all CTE outputs of the same temporal type and fractional precision.

=== tm-e3: GREATEST of a DATE and a DATETIME scalar CTE is refused ===
Error handling: RPE
ronsql_cli caught exception: A CTE output that is a MIN or MAX of a DATE, DATETIME, TIME, TIMESTAMP or YEAR column can be used in an aggregate only as the argument of MIN or MAX, or in a GREATEST or LEAST whose arguments are all CTE outputs of the same temporal type and fractional precision.

=== tm-e4: GREATEST of a DATE scalar CTE and a constant is refused ===
Error handling: RPE
ronsql_cli caught exception: A CTE output that is a MIN or MAX of a DATE, DATETIME, TIME, TIMESTAMP or YEAR column can be used in an aggregate only as the argument of MIN or MAX, or in a GREATEST or LEAST whose arguments are all CTE outputs of the same temporal type and fractional precision.

=== tm-e5: a DATETIME(3) MAX compared with YYYYMMDD is refused ===
Error handling: RPE
ronsql_cli caught exception: A CTE output that is a MIN or MAX of a DATE, DATETIME, TIME, TIMESTAMP or YEAR column can be compared only with a valid date or time string (a TIME string with at most the column's fractional digits), or with an integer written YYYYMMDD for a DATE, YYYYMMDDhhmmss for a DATETIME or TIMESTAMP, hhmmss for a TIME and YYYY for a YEAR.

=== tm-e6: a TIME(2) MIN compared with three fractional digits is refused ===
Error handling: RPE
ronsql_cli caught exception: A CTE output that is a MIN or MAX of a DATE, DATETIME, TIME, TIMESTAMP or YEAR column can be compared only with a valid date or time string (a TIME string with at most the column's fractional digits), or with an integer written YYYYMMDD for a DATE, YYYYMMDDhhmmss for a DATETIME or TIMESTAMP, hhmmss for a TIME and YYYY for a YEAR.

=== tm-e7: WHERE GREATEST of TIME outputs compared with a string is refused ===
Error handling: RPE
ronsql_cli caught exception: GREATEST or LEAST of a CTE output that is a MIN or MAX of a TIME column, compared with a string, is not supported. Compare with an integer hhmmss, or compare each CTE output with the string.
